      <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>A $5,000 Good Energy air sealing rebate is available if you reduce air leakage from 3 or more air changes to 1.5 air changes or less (@50Pa). This can be achieved through a deep energy retrofit with comprehensive air sealing details performed on walls, ceilings and all building penetrations. Houses with low levels of air leakage require a balanced ventilation system, such as a heat recovery ventilator (HRV), to provide fresh air to the home and to exhaust stale air. See ventilation system comments for Good Energy HRV rebates.
</airSeal>
                <ceilingsCathedral>
The insulation in your insulated flat roof was assessed at R-32. Because the amount of insulation in your insulated flat roof has been assessed as being greater than R-25 but less than or equal to R-35, a grant of $200 is available for adding insulation to reach R-40 or more.  
</ceilingsCathedral>
            </RURComments>
      <GreenerHomes basementSlabInsulated="false" moistureProofCrawlSpace="false" waterproofing="false" roofingMembrane="false" minR10ContinuousExposedFloors="false" backwaterValve="false" sumpPump="false" smartThermostats="false" remoteCommunities="false" evaluationCost="">
